 "caption": "97% of learners quit. Your badges didn't help. Comment 1, 2 or 3: which one is your training missing?\n\nMIT and Harvard tracked course completion in their own online courses for 6 years. In 2017-18 only 3.1% of participants finished, and the rate never really improved.\n\nGames? Opposite problem. And employee training can steal all 3 of their tricks:\n\n1. Feedback in seconds, not at the final quiz\n2. A goal you can see from level 1\n3. A challenge that grows as you get better\n\nA badge is the sticker. The game is the box.\n\nSource: Reich & Ruipérez-Valiente, \"The MOOC pivot\", Science 363 (2019).\n\n#gamification #elearning #learninganddevelopment #instructionaldesign #gamedesign"
}